Subject: util/disk_cache: add a Windows multi-file backend

Upstream Mesa (main at 66e82ef1, 2026-11-25, and 26.2.2) refuses
-Dshader-cache=enabled on Windows and leaves disk_cache_os.c as
"TODO: implement disk cache support on windows". This adds that backend.

- The entry format helpers (parse_and_validate_cache_item,
  create_cache_item_header_and_blob) and the Fossilize/database wrappers are
  shared; only file system calls differ.
- The Windows backend keeps the POSIX multi-file layout and entry format:
  <dir>/mesa_shader_cache/<2 hex>/<62 hex>, written to a .tmp file and
  renamed into place, plus the shared "index" file (size and key index).
  An exclusive share mode on the .tmp file stands in for flock(); rename()
  never replaces an existing entry, so the size accounting stays right.
- It uses only C runtime calls and AppContainer-safe Win32 calls
  (CreateFileMappingFromApp/MapViewOfFileFromApp when WINAPI_FAMILY_APP).
- The directory must be named by MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR: a packaged process
  has no per-user default location, so without it the cache is disabled.
  MESA_SHADER_CACHE_MAX_SIZE and MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE work as upstream.
- On Windows the meson 'shader-cache' option stays off for 'auto' and is
  built with -Dshader-cache=enabled.

